"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[9111],{89111:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"schemaVersion":1,"locale":"en","slug":"gajd-1-iis","title":"Guide 1. Launching an IIA-3: A Step-by-Step Roadmap from Choosing a Broker to the First Purchase","sourceFingerprint":"e0f55a5ddf6f8b8f85c14bfe79e3a972ea5269db4c37614f2d39adab7fa85d5b","blocks":[{"id":"b001","markdown":"# Workshop: Launching IIS-3. A Step-by-Step Route from Broker Selection to Your First Exchange-Traded Asset"},{"id":"b002","markdown":"*Completion time: ~25 minutes for actions + 1–2 business days for registration*  \\n*MakeCash Academy \xb7 makecash.pro*  \\n*Volume II: Capital Protection: 20 Years Against Inflation*"},{"id":"b003","markdown":"> \\"Investment discipline begins not with searching for rare skyrocketing stocks, but with a properly set up tax-advantaged account, an automated recurring payment, and a firm commitment not to touch the capital for at least five years.\\""},{"id":"b004","markdown":"## \uD83E\uDDED Investor Roadmap"},{"id":"b005","markdown":"Transitioning from theory to a real brokerage account often causes paralysis due to the abundance of terms, tariffs, and buttons in the interface. This workshop breaks down the entire process into eight clear steps, allowing you to set up your personal investment infrastructure without unnecessary fuss."},{"id":"b006","markdown":"### Step 1. Pre-launch Audit: Are You Ready to Invest?"},{"id":"b007","markdown":"Before transferring money to the exchange, check against the financial hygiene rules from the first volume of our handbook:"},{"id":"b008","markdown":"- **No toxic debt.** Credit card debt or payday loans eat away returns faster than any investment.\\n- **An established emergency fund.** Savings for unforeseen circumstances (three to six months of basic expenses) are kept separately — in a high-yield savings account or a liquidity fund.\\n- **A planning horizon of 5+ years.** Money directed to a Type-3 Individual Investment Account will not be needed for everyday living over the next five-year period."},{"id":"b009","markdown":"> ⚠️ **Important detail:** If you already have an old-style contract open (IIS-1 or IIS-2 opened before January 1, 2024), you cannot register a parallel IIS-3. You have two options: close the old account (if the three-year term has elapsed) or officially convert it into an IIS-3 with partial credit for the prior holding period through your broker\'s customer support."},{"id":"b010","markdown":"### Step 2. Selecting an Intermediary: 3 Filters of Broker Reliability"},{"id":"b011","markdown":"Don\'t chase complex terminals. For systematic long-term purchases, it is sufficient to rely on three basic criteria:"},{"id":"b012","markdown":"| Screening Criterion | What to Look For | Why It Matters |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **1. Regulatory license** | Company\'s presence in the official register of the Bank of Russia (verified on cbr.ru). | A guarantee that your assets are legally protected and held in an official depository. |\\n| **2. Fee structure** | No monthly maintenance fee for account management and depository services. Transaction fee within 0.03–0.3%. | With purchases 1–2 times a month, a fixed monthly fee of 150–300 ₽ can destroy the returns of a small portfolio. |\\n| **3. Ecosystem seamlessness** | The broker operates within the bank whose card you use regularly. | Instant and free deposit/withdrawal of funds without interbank fees or delays. |"},{"id":"b013","markdown":"> \uD83D\uDEE1️ **Capital preservation guarantees:** Starting in 2026, a state insurance mechanism of up to 1,400,000 ₽ for funds will come into effect for IIS-3 in the event of a broker\'s bankruptcy (similar to deposit insurance for bank deposits by the DIA). However, broker participation in this system is voluntary — be sure to confirm with customer support whether the company is included in the insurance fund."},{"id":"b014","markdown":"### Step 3. Registering the Account and Starting the Five-Year Timer"},{"id":"b015","markdown":"In the mobile bank or investment app, navigate to the \\"Open a new account\\" tab and select \\"Individual Investment Account\\"."},{"id":"b016","markdown":"1. Fill out the application form (usually populated automatically via your client profile or Gosuslugi).\\n2. Confirm the signing of the agreement with an SMS code.\\n3. Wait for the opening notification (the procedure takes anywhere from 15 minutes to a couple of business days)."},{"id":"b017","markdown":"> \uD83D\uDCCC **Make a note in your notebook:** Record the exact date the agreement was opened. This specific calendar day is the starting point for the minimum five-year asset holding period."},{"id":"b018","markdown":"### Step 4. Depositing Funds: The December Calendar Trap"},{"id":"b019","markdown":"Funding the balance is carried out via a regular internal transfer from a current bank account or debit card directly within the broker\'s interface."},{"id":"b020","markdown":"- The tax deduction is calculated on the **amount actually credited** within the calendar year (from January 1 to December 31).\\n- **Year-end trap:** If you decide to top up your account to claim the benefit for the current year, make the transfer **no later than December 10–15**. Payments sent in the final days before the holidays may not land in the brokerage account until January due to interbank clearing, pushing the deduction forward by an entire year."},{"id":"b021","markdown":"### Step 5. Purchasing Your First Exchange-Traded Instrument"},{"id":"b022","markdown":"To start, there is no need to try to guess future growth leaders. It is enough to purchase a reliable collective instrument — for example, a money market fund (LQDT or its direct equivalents from major providers) or an index fund covering the entire stock market (tickers of funds tracking the MOEX index)."},{"id":"b023","markdown":"```\\n[Search for ticker in the app] ➜ [Analyze management company fee] ➜ [Select order type] ➜ [Buy]\\n```"},{"id":"b024","markdown":"1. **Enter the ticker** in the search bar of the trading app (for example, `LQDT`).\\n2. **Check the instrument card:** review the total expenses of the management company (they are automatically deducted from net asset value).\\n3. **Specify the volume:** enter the desired number of units or lots.\\n4. **Order type:** \\n   - *Market order* is executed instantly at the current market ask price.\\n   - *Limit order* is triggered strictly at your specified price or better.\\n5. **Transaction time:** make purchases during the main daytime trading session of the Moscow Exchange (from 10:00 to 18:40 Moscow time), when liquidity is highest and the spread (the difference between bid and ask prices) is minimal."},{"id":"b025","markdown":"### Step 6. Process Automation: Investing on Autopilot"},{"id":"b026","markdown":"The investor\'s main enemy is forgetfulness and trying to time the \\"ideal entry point\\"."},{"id":"b027","markdown":"- Set up an **automatic payment** in your banking app: the day after your salary is credited, a fixed amount (for example, 5 000, 10 000, or 30 000 ₽) should automatically transfer to your IIS-3.\\n- If your broker supports an asset auto-buy feature, enable it for your chosen fund. If there is no such option, set a recurring monthly calendar reminder: log in for 2 minutes and tap the \\"Buy\\" button."},{"id":"b028","markdown":"### Step 7. Claiming the Tax Refund"},{"id":"b029","markdown":"Money withheld by the state as personal income tax from your official salary can be refunded to your bank account as early as the beginning of the following year:"},{"id":"b030","markdown":"* **Proactive (simplified) format:** in the first quarter, the broker independently submits data to the Federal Tax Service. A pre-filled application appears in your taxpayer account on `nalog.gov.ru`. All you need to do is log in, verify the bank details for the transfer, and sign it with an electronic signature in one click. The funds arrive within 30 days.\\n* **Filing via 3-NDFL tax return:** if the pre-filled consent has not been generated automatically by March–April, generate an electronic tax return manually through the same personal account, attaching the broker\'s cash flow statement. The statute of limitations for the refund is 3 years."},{"id":"b031","markdown":"> \uD83D\uDCA1 **Snowball effect:** never spend the refunded personal income tax on everyday consumption. Deposit it back into the IIS-3, unleashing the power of compound interest on government money."},{"id":"b032","markdown":"### Step 8. Maintaining the Five-Year Horizon"},{"id":"b033","markdown":"IIS-3 is a long-distance tool with strict withdrawal rules:"},{"id":"b034","markdown":"1. **Prohibition of partial withdrawals.** You cannot withdraw 10 000 or 50 000 ₽ while leaving the rest to work. Any partial withdrawal is treated by the tax authority as early termination of the account.\\n2. **The cost of error.** If you terminate the agreement before five years, you will have to return every penny of the deductions received to the state, as well as pay penalties for each day of using that money.\\n3. **Exceptional cases.** The legislation allows early withdrawal of funds without closing the account or forfeiting tax benefits solely to pay for expensive medical treatment from the approved list of the Government of the Russian Federation.\\n4. **Maturity closure rule:** once the 5 years have passed, it is more advantageous to close the account in the first months of a new calendar year — no contribution deduction is granted for the calendar year in which the agreement is actually terminated."},{"id":"b035","markdown":"## \uD83E\uDDEE Back-of-the-Napkin Calculation: The Power of Reinvesting Deductions"},{"id":"b036","markdown":"Let\'s see what real benefit disciplined reinvestment of the tax refund brings compared to simple accumulation in a regular brokerage account, with a contribution of **400 000 ₽ per year** (the maximum deduction base) and a stable personal income tax rate of 13%."},{"id":"b037","markdown":"*Baseline conditions: annual contribution of 400 000 ₽, conservative portfolio return of 12% per annum, term of 5 years.*"},{"id":"b038","markdown":"| Investment Year | Investor\'s Annual Contribution | PIT Refund for Previous Year (13%) | Total Contribution with Reinvestment | Portfolio Balance at Year-End (incl. 12% return) |\\n| :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |\\n| **Year 1** | 400 000 ₽ | 0 ₽ | 400 000 ₽ | 448 000 ₽ |\\n| **Year 2** | 400 000 ₽ | +52 000 ₽ | 452 000 ₽ | 1 008 000 ₽ |\\n| **Year 3** | 400 000 ₽ | +52 000 ₽ | 452 000 ₽ | 1 635 200 ₽ |\\n| **Year 4** | 400 000 ₽ | +52 000 ₽ | 452 000 ₽ | 2 337 664 ₽ |\\n| **Year 5** | 400 000 ₽ | +52 000 ₽ | 452 000 ₽ | 3 124 424 ₽ |"},{"id":"b039","markdown":"**Final result after 5 years:**\\n- Own funds deposited: **2 000 000 ₽**.\\n- Tax refunds received and added to the market: **208 000 ₽** (plus the right to a deduction for year 5 in the amount of another 52 000 ₽).\\n- Total capital value in the account exceeds **3.12 million ₽**.\\n- All investment gains on the IIS-3 are exempt from personal income tax upon closure (within the limit of up to 30 million ₽)."},{"id":"b040","markdown":"## ✍️ Step-by-Step Investor Checklist"},{"id":"b041","markdown":"Check off the steps completed in practice:"},{"id":"b042","markdown":"- [ ] **Personal reserve is secure:** a 3–6 month cushion is kept separately from exchange accounts.\\n- [ ] **Old agreements checked:** confirmed absence of open old-type IIS accounts (prior to 2024) or the procedure to convert them to IIS-3 has been initiated.\\n- [ ] **Broker verified:** CBR license checked, a platform without monthly account maintenance fees selected.\\n- [ ] **IIS-3 officially opened:** contract conclusion date recorded in the organizer (start of the five-year withdrawal moratorium).\\n- [ ] **First deposit made:** funds credited to the balance (taking into account the December 15 deadline for the current year).\\n- [ ] **First exchange asset purchased:** trade executed during the main trading session via a limit or market order.\\n- [ ] **Auto-payment set up:** a recurring deposit template set up in online banking for payday.\\n- [ ] **Calendar reminder:** a reminder created on the phone for February of next year — \\"Check pre-filled deduction in nalog.gov.ru account\\"."}],"terms":[{"id":"filtry-brokera","term":"Broker reliability filters","definition":"checking the Bank of Russia license, tariff plans, and the absence of maintenance fees."},{"id":"avtopokupka","term":"Auto-purchase","definition":"setting up automatic regular purchases of exchange-traded assets on deposit days."},{"id":"pyatiletnij-taymer","term":"Five-year timer","definition":"the minimum holding period for an IIA-3 to retain tax benefits."}],"quizzes":[{"id":"q1","q":"What is the primary criterion when choosing a broker to open an IIA-3 account that protects against fraud risks?","options":["The broker is listed in the official register of licensed participants of the Bank of Russia","An advertisement promising to double your capital in 6 months","Company registration in a zero-tax offshore jurisdiction"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Safe investing is only possible through a licensed broker included in the official register of the Bank of Russia."},{"id":"q2","q":"What happens to the tax deductions received if an IIA-3 is closed before the minimum 5-year period expires?","options":["Nothing, the investor keeps all received money","All received deductions must be returned to the state along with penalties accrued for each day","The funds in the account are completely confiscated by the state"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Upon early closure of an IIA-3, the tax authority recovers all received deductions with daily penalty charges applied."},{"id":"q3","q":"Which exchange-traded instrument is optimal for a first purchase on an IIA-3 to safely park funds amid high interest rates?","options":["High-risk third-tier company stocks using leverage","A money market exchange-traded fund (LQDT) or short-term fixed-coupon OFZ bonds","Volatility index futures"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Money market funds accrue income daily at the RUSFAR rate without price fluctuation risks."}],"officialSources":[]}')}}]);